<title>POLAND: BWR shareholders set issue price PLN 3.81.</title>
<headline>BWR shareholders set issue price PLN 3.81.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Poland's Bank Wspolpracy Regionalnej SA (BWR) approved its new issue of 1.7 million shares and set an issue price at 3.81 zlotys per share, BWR said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the shares would be earmarked for three investors which would pay with real estate for the shares. The property involved was in the towns of Nowa Sol, Krakow and Tarnow.</p>
<p>BWR earlier said the ex-rights issue would likely take place in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>BWR currently has 12,502,802 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
